{"timestamp":"2026-05-30T21:50:44.034Z","level":"info","source":"model","message":"response","data":{"model":"qwen36-35b","text":"\n\nI've loaded the **blueprint.md** file. This is the architectural blueprint for **VoidRift** — a decoupled, local-first AI engineering harness with an interactive TUI.\n\nHere's a high-level overview of what's covered:\n\n## Core Architecture\n- **5 architectural pillars** (local-first, model-agnostic, etc.)\n- **6-layer execution flow** with a central event bus\n- **Three-tier model router** with `flash` (scout), `utility` (collaborator), and `dense` (architect) tiers\n\n## Key Subsystems\n1. **Container** — workspace isolation\n2. **Model Connectivity** — multi-model routing\n3. **Capability** — tool/capability management\n4. **Security** — async confirmation gates\n5. **Operator Interface (TUI)** — interactive terminal UI\n6. **Agent Session** — 3-partition context manager\n\n## Context Management\n- **3-Partition Context**: `Governance` (immutable rules), `Workspace` (semi-dynamic), `Work` (volatile history)\n- Optimized for LLM prompt cache reuse (~90%)\n\n## Key Files & Configs\n- Global config: `~/.","toolCalls":[],"usage":{"promptTokens":1626,"completionTokens":607,"totalTokens":2233}}}
